{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"Career windows (job change, promotion) from the 10th house, its lord and the karakas Sun and Saturn, 6th, 11th and 2nd supporting; KP group 2, 6, 10, 11. Windows over `years` (1 to 20, default 5) from `fromDate`, cut at every Vimshottari period change (`level` pratyantar by default, or antar) and every Jupiter or Saturn sign change. Each window has `score`, its `components` (dasha, transit, kp) and every rule that fired, with `basis` (classical, modern, kp) and a `source` key into `sources`. Double transit (K.N.\n\n[Group: Vedic]\n[Endpoint: POST /v1/vedic/timing/career]\n[Cost: 50 credits (Tier 3)]","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"body":{"allOf":[{"additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{},{"type":"null"}]},"description":"Birth data for a single natal chart. Required: date (YYYY-MM-DD), time (HH:mm:ss), latitude and longitude in decimal degrees. The short forms lat, lon, lng and tz are rejected with 400 INVALID_FIELD; pass the full names. timezoneOffset is hours from UTC and defaults to 0, meaning UTC; send timezone instead (an IANA name such as Europe/Kyiv, or auto) and the offset for that date is worked out, summer time included. city is a display label only: nothing here geocodes it, so it never stands in for coordinates. houseSystem is a single house-system letter, P by default; a name such as \"Placidus\" is refused, and the case matters because I and i are two different Sunshine systems.","properties":{"ayanamsa":{"description":"Sidereal school by name. Lahiri when omitted. Equivalent to ayanamsaId; send either.","enum":["fagan-bradley","lahiri","de-luce","raman","krishnamurti","kp","yukteshwar","jn-bhasin","true-citra","djwhal-khul"],"type":"string"},"ayanamsaId":{"type":["number","null"]},"city":{"default":"","type":"string"},"cosmogram":{"type":"boolean"},"date":{"pattern":"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$","type":"string"},"houseSystem":{"default":"P","enum":["P","K","R","C","E","W","B","M","O","A","T","V","D","F","G","H","I","i","L","N","Q","S","U","X","Y"],"type":"string"},"latitude":{"maximum":90,"minimum":-90,"type":"number"},"longitude":{"maximum":180,"minimum":-180,"type":"number"},"name":{"default":"","type":"string"},"time":{"pattern":"^\\d{2}:\\d{2}(:\\d{2})?$","type":"string"},"timezone":{"description":"IANA zone name such as Europe/Kyiv, or auto to look the zone up from latitude and longitude. The server takes the offset that zone kept at this local date and time, summer time included, and uses it in place of timezoneOffset. A clock time that happened twice takes the first occurrence; one skipped when clocks went forward takes the offset from before the change. Abbreviations such as EST are refused. Before 1970 the tz database is not reliable for every place, so send timezoneOffset when the local clock is known.","type":"string"},"timezoneOffset":{"anyOf":[{"maximum":14,"minimum":-14,"type":"number"},{"type":"null"}],"default":0,"description":"Hours from UTC at the given moment, not minutes. Fractional zones are hours too: 5.5 for India, 5.75 for Nepal, -3.5 for Newfoundland. Defaults to 0, meaning UTC. Ignored when timezone is sent."},"zodiacType":{"enum":["tropical","sidereal"],"type":"string"}},"required":["date","time","latitude","longitude"],"type":"object"},{"additionalProperties":{"anyOf":[{},{"type":"null"}]},"properties":{"fromDate":{"description":"Start of the span, YYYY-MM-DD (UTC). Today when omitted.","pattern":"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$","type":"string"},"kp":{"description":"Add KP significators (Placidus cusps): each dasha lord scores for the houses of the area's KP group it signifies. Default false.","type":"boolean"},"level":{"description":"Finest dasha level that cuts the windows. pratyantar (default): maha, antar and pratyantar lords are scored. antar: maha and antar only, fewer and longer windows.",